From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 17:06:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] input, dialogs, AudioEngine: add what a hosted client needs

A Wayland client hosted by Kodi takes keyboard input, may use Kodi's
on-screen keyboard and may hand Kodi encoded audio. Let a keyboard
event handler take events before Kodi translates them into actions,
tell whether a keyboard with letter keys is attached on GBM, let a
keyboard dialog derived from the generic one choose its own window,
and unpack the frame of an IEC 61937 burst.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
